# UI package (`@app/ui` → `packages/ui`)

Base UI consumed per subpath: `import { Button } from "@app/ui/button"`.
Public import paths stay flat; source files live in category folders.

## Source layout

```
packages/ui/src/
  lib/           cn + helpers
  primitives/    shadcn building blocks (button, card, dialog, table, …)
  shell/         app chrome (brand, nav-item, site-header, sidebar,
                 sidebar-shell, navbar-shell, auth-shell, user-menu-button)
  composites/    higher-level patterns (data-table, page-header, empty-state, confirm-dialog, …)
```

## Rules

- Every new component file MUST be registered in `packages/ui/package.json` under `exports` — without that entry the subpath import fails
- Keep it app-neutral: no `@/` imports, no product copy, no domain/tenant knowledge. A component that needs product copy or business logic belongs in `apps/web/src/domains/<domain>/components/` instead
- Primitives are shadcn-generated — restyle through variants/tokens, don't hand-rewrite them. Shell and composite pieces stay generic
- Colors come only from the CSS variables (`--primary`, `--background`, …) that the web app's ThemeProvider writes — never hardcode a color, or theming breaks
- `cn` lives at `packages/ui/src/lib/utils.ts` (`@app/ui/lib/utils`)
- Only add a component here when a generic UI shape repeats across pages; one-off UI stays in the app
- Put new files in the matching category folder (`primitives/` / `shell/` / `composites/`)
